detaileddescription.para:
Useful for inserting absolute symbols into a JITDylib. E.g.: JITDylib&JD=...;
SymbolStringPtrFoo=...;
ExecutorSymbolDefFooSym=...;
if(autoErr=JD.define(absoluteSymbols({
{Foo,FooSym},
{Bar,BarSym}
})))
returnErr;

Useful for defining symbol aliases.: E.g., given a JITDylib JD containing symbols "foo" and "bar", we can define aliases "baz" (for "foo") and "qux" (for "bar") with: SymbolStringPtrBaz=...;
SymbolStringPtrQux=...;
if(autoErr=JD.define(symbolAliases({
{Baz,{Foo,JITSymbolFlags::Exported}},
{Qux,{Bar,JITSymbolFlags::Weak}}}))
returnErr;
